On Mon, 4 Jul 2005, Jym wrote:

> OK, following the recent discution about spell hunger for mages, and
> since I have time to lose after my ascension, here comes the reduce
> spell hunger patch.

OK, time for the next version :-)

Spell hunger now depend on both class and race, according to the following
principle :

A "hunger intelligence" is computed, and spell hunger is reduced by 10%
for each point over 15 (that is 100% spell hunger at 15 or less, 50% at
20, 0% at 25). Since spell hunger goes by 10s, this is fairly nice :-)

The hunger intelligence is :
10 for all fighter classes (B, C, S, U, V, Y) whatever their race (no
spell hunger reduction).
INT+5 for wizards, not modified by race (the wiz training takes precedence
over the racial data) (still half hunger at 15, but 0 hunger at 20 rather
than 17, and reduced hunger starting at 11).
INT+3 for mages (reduction from 13 to 22 real INT).
INT for Necro and Priest.
INT-3 for Arc and Heal.
INT-4 for Ra and Ro.
INT-5 for Kn, Monk and Tourist.

Then, hunger intelligence is modified by the race (except for wiz and
fighters):
Human: no modif.
Orc, dwarf : -3 (bad at magic).
Elf, drow : +2 (good at magic).
Gnome, hobbits : +1 (why didn't I put +0 ?)
Doppelgangers: set at 10 (they use magic for polyself, not for
spellcasting. Since this is done after class check, doppel wiz still get
their bonuses).
Vampire, Werewolf : +3 is lower that actual INT (only usefull to
compensate a class malus) (they live because magic exists, so they're more
aware of it than their fellow).

Don't know if that is too unbalanced or not, any remark and suggestion
welcome.

Maybe I should take spell skill into account.

